<title>FRANCE: Juppe repeats EMU decision will be political.</title>
<headline>Juppe repeats EMU decision will be political.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Departing French Prime Minister Alain Juppe repeated on Tuesday that the decision on which countries would take part in a single European currency would be political.</p>
<p>Speaking on RTL radio Juppe said: &quot;Everyone knows well that when the European Council meets in March or April 1998, and when it looks at the situation, the move to a single currency will be a political decision.&quot;</p>
<p>He repeated there should be a flexible interpretation of the Maastricht deficit criterion.</p>
</text>
